---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { CsvColumnMapTool } from "../../components/tools/csv-column-map/CsvColumnMapTool";
import "../../components/tools/tool-surface.css";
---
<BaseLayout title="CSV Column Map / Reorder" description="Select, rename, and reorder CSV columns locally with an explicit output schema preview.">
  <article class="tool-page"><header class="tool-heading"><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Workbench</a> / Data</nav><p class="eyebrow">Data cleanup</p><h1>CSV Column Map / Reorder</h1><p class="lede">Choose source columns by position, rename them, reorder them, and inspect the exact output schema before applying the transformation.</p><div class="trust-strip" role="note"><strong>Runs on this device.</strong><span>Your CSV stays local; dropped columns and blank-filled ragged cells are disclosed before/after output.</span></div></header><CsvColumnMapTool client:load /><section class="method-card"><h2>Mapping contract</h2><ul><li>Input columns are identified by zero-ambiguity source position even when header names repeat.</li><li>Output header names must be non-empty and unique.</li><li>Dropping a source column is explicit and visible in the schema preview.</li><li>If a ragged row lacks a selected source cell, the output cell is blank and the filled-cell count is reported.</li></ul></section></article>
</BaseLayout>
